;;; nodecode-box-runs-a-checkout-dump — define-memory written 2026-11-23
(in-package :nodecode.evolved)

(define-memory nodecode-box-runs-a-checkout-dump
  "Box nay DANG CHAY ban build tu checkout /home/boxes/nodecode (0.1.16+c78fef6 tu 23/11), khong phai ban cai tu channel: `current` cung tro vao dump cua checkout. Cap nhat = merge upstream/main, `just release`, cai beside, roi reload qua user unit."
  :type :project)
;; why: 2026-11-23 the operator asked to update from the root repo. `nodecode update' answered "a8dcf1cef runs at the next launch: this image refused it live", while the serving pid was /home/boxes/nodecode/nodecode -- readlink -f /proc/<serve>/exe and `ps -o args'. So the installed-release route is not how this home runs; two launch routes exist (the unit's ExecStart names `current', and a shell whose own dump is a checkout starts its own path), so `current' and the checkout must both name the same build or a restart disagrees with itself.
;; route that works: cd /home/boxes/nodecode && git fetch upstream && git merge upstream/main --no-edit (10 box commits on 60db5cd91 merged cleanly onto 4d5e26a, no conflicts) && export PATH=$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH && just release -> "nodecode 0.1.16+<merge hash>"; then install beside: mkdir ~/.local/share/nodecode/<short>; cp nodecode, cp -a src, README.txt; chmod 700 the binary; ln -sfn <short> ~/.local/share/nodecode/current. ~/.sbclrc loads quicklisp, so the justfile resolves cl+ssl on SBCL 2.6.0 (the toolchain build-nodecode-here set up).
;; reload without killing the answer in flight: a script started by `setsid nohup sh -c 'sleep 45; script'` that TERMs the pid written in ~/.nodecode/history.db.owner, then `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/$(id -u) systemctl --user restart nodecode-gateway.service`, then prints `nodecode gateway status` and each `nodecode serve` pid's /proc/<pid>/exe. Without XDG_RUNTIME_DIR systemctl answers "Failed to connect to bus: No medium found" -- nodecode-gateway.service is a USER unit (uid 1002 here), not a system one. The gateway alone is not enough: it says "waiting" for a serve that a client started, so the serve must be stopped for the new build to be the one that boots.
;; way back: ln -sfn 60db5cd91 current (the official nightly dir is still there), or git checkout 8d08e08 + just release.
